  "title": "what to do when a box outside a group falls between two boxes inside it",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "Q3 of docs/plans/groups-in-the-layout/PLAN.md, plus a count over every graph file under docs/plans and ~/.cache/agent-graphs",
  "explanation": "Collapsing a group into one unit can turn a straight chain into a loop, and that is a new failure mode this design introduces rather than one it inherits. [Letting it render](#let-it-render) leans on the loop breaker the layout already has and draws one arrow running backwards through the boundary. [Refusing the write](#refuse-the-write) makes the agent fix its group before anything is drawn, at the cost of rejecting a graph that is otherwise legal. The count is the thing to look at: this is not a corner case.",
